{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hn2Z71EGNyrooN4xCRmXzx","type":"tool_result","content":"739: * 5. INPUT  keyboard, mouse, gamepad, touch stick, on-screen buttons\n741: *    'Pad0'..'Pad15' (standard gamepad buttons). Every action also accepts\n742: *    'Act:<name>' so DOM buttons with data-act=\"<name>\" work automatically.\n761:     *  left stick after the dead zone; padAim: its right stick, or null when centered; padPrev: which gamepad buttons\n775:     *  anywhere on the screen but the buttons steers by drag(), with no stick drawn: a shooter's ship that follows the\n856:     *  (DOM buttons with data-act, tap, hold) */\n931:   * On-screen buttons for phones and tablets (shown on touch screens; the player's settings can show them always or hide\n954:  /** where the touch buttons cover the screen, in screen pixels { x0, y0, x1, y1 } (the same space as r.W and r.H), or\n964:  /** build the touch buttons again from the player's settings (touch, hand, touchSize, touchOpacity) */\n998:    if (code.startsWith('Pad')) { this.lastDevice = 'gamepad'; this.aimSource = 'pad'; }\n1016:  down(a) { const m = this.map[a]; if (!m) { this._check(a); return false; } if (this._suppressed.has(a)) return false; for (const c of m) if (this.held.has(c)) return true; return false; }\n1018:  pressed(a) { if (!this.map[a]) this._check(a); return !this._suppressed.has(a) && this._now.has(a); }\n1023:    if (this.pressed(a)) return true;\n1135:  tick(dt) {\n1145:      this.padPrev.forEach((on, i) => { if (on) this.release('Pad' + i); });\n1158:      p.buttons.forEach((b, i) => { const on = b.pressed; if (on && !this.padPrev[i]) this.press('Pad' + i); if (!on && this.padPrev[i]) this.release('Pad' + i); this.padPrev[i] = on; });\n1260:const padCode = c => c.startsWith('Pad');\n1261:/* a standard gamepad's buttons by position (0 bottom, 1 right, 2 left, 3 top, 4-7 shoulders and triggers, 8 back, 9 start,\n2286:   * - corner, backGesture: corner: the menu and full-screen buttons (top right); backGesture: a\n2307:    // every listener the engine adds to the window, the document, the canvas and its buttons goes through this: dispose() removes them all\n2330:     *  focus sits (above a phone's touch buttons: [0, -40]); x, y: the camera's position in projected pixels (its\n2508:   *  full-screen choice kept, a phone's first tap going full screen, the corner buttons and the menu screens */\n2557:  /** where the corner's buttons (menu and full screen, top right; the touch START) cover the screen, in screen pixels\n2565:  /** show or hide the corner buttons: shown while the game isn't being played (a title, a game over, a pause without\n2567:   *  engine's touch buttons it is their START); hidden under an open menu screen (its close button is there) */\n2769:   * the document, the canvas and the buttons, the touch controls, the GPU lighting's canvas) and close the sound. Tests and\n3001:  touch: { group: 'Touch', label: 'Touch buttons', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Automatic'], ['on', 'Always'], ['off', 'Hidden']], apply: g => g.input._touchSync() },\n3082:  /** game.fullscreen: the whole page full screen (the game, its menus and buttons), where the browser can */\n3113:/* the corner buttons: menu and full screen, 44 px, top right inside the safe area (Game._cornerSync shows them); on a\n3595:// one step of a sequence, 'down+right' or 'attack' or 'down+attack': the directions it holds (bits) and the buttons pressed\n3600: * exactly as it says (up, down, left, right; 'neutral' for none) as they change to that, its buttons pressed. A cheat\n3664:const KEY_HALVES = {   // each half's moves, its buttons in order (the preset's other actions take them in turn) and its menu keys\n3665:  left: { up: ['KeyW'], down: ['KeyS'], left: ['KeyA'], right: ['KeyD'], buttons: [['KeyF'], ['KeyG'], ['KeyH'], ['KeyR'], ['KeyT'], ['KeyY'], ['KeyV'], ['KeyB']], start: ['Digit1'], pause: ['Escape', 'Digit1'], confirm: ['KeyF'], cancel: ['KeyG'] },\n3666:  right: { up: ['ArrowUp'], down: ['ArrowDown'], left: ['ArrowLeft'], right: ['ArrowRight'], buttons: [['Period', 'Numpad1'], ['Slash', 'Numpad2'], ['Comma', 'Numpad3'], ['KeyL', 'Numpad4'], ['Semicolon', 'Numpad5'], ['Quote', 'Numpad6'], ['KeyK', 'Numpad7'], ['KeyM', 'Numpad8']],\n3669:/** a preset for half a keyboard ('left' or 'right'): its moves and menu keys, the preset's other actions on its buttons\n3674:  for (const a in P) out[a] = (H[a] || H.buttons[k++] || []).concat(P[a].filter(c => padCode(c)));\n3699:  q.lastDevice = q.device; if (q.pad !== null) { q.tick(0); q.consumeAll(); }   // (the buttons held as it joins, its Start among them, are no presses)\n3766:    const on = !!(p.buttons[9] && p.buttons[9].pressed), prev = (game._joinPrev || (game._joinPrev = {}))[p.index]; game._joinPrev[p.index] = on;\n8895:    if (t && x + w > t.x0 && x < t.x1 && y + h > t.y0) {   // clear of the touch buttons: beside them where it fits, else above them\n9089: *    the game passes values in every step and callbacks for the buttons, and it reaches the game only through those and\n  flashes: { group: 'Comfort', label: 'Screen flashes', type: 'slider', value: 1 },\n  bindings: { group: 'Controls', type: 'bindings', value: () => ({}), apply: (g, v) => { g.input.bindings = v; } },\n  deadzone: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Stick dead zone', type: 'slider', value: .18, min: .05, max: .5, step: .01, apply: (g, v) => { g.input.deadzone = v; } },\n  invertY: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Invert aim up and down', type: 'toggle', value: false, apply: (g, v) => { g.input.invertAimY = !!v; } },\n  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { g.input.glyphs = v; } },\n  rumble: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Vibration', type: 'slider', value: .6, apply: (g, v) 