{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghtJfonUxWxbUvCJQaUb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016CdeyqL1hX1BBmMeVV827E","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050317__x1f94fb/work && cat > exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:03:17\",\n    \"source\": \"TrackMania 2003 (Nadeo)\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Racing (arcade time attack)\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Third-person chase camera; orbiting camera on the title and attract screens\",\n    \"tech\": \"my-3D2dge 2D engine and 3D engine v0.85.2 (commit 4390a98), three.js r182 (WebGL 2 fallback), Rapier 0.19.3, esbuild 0.25.12, playwright-core 1.63.0 (checks)\",\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's toon 3D style with ink outlines and pixel-art UI, all drawn by code (pen parts, no image files)\",\n    \"animation\": \"Code-driven car, checkpoint gate and camera motion; no rig animation\",\n    \"audio\": \"Engine songs and sound effects synthesised in code; no voices yet (no Animalese)\",\n    \"online\": \"none\",\n    \"testing\": \"Headless Node suites (track format, car physics, bot finishing every road, run rules, scene flow, modes) run by one command; Playwright boot and screenshot checks of the built file\",\n    \"research\": \"none\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\",\n    \"usage\": \"unknown\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"About eight real bugs were caught; three were critical: the steering sign (no bot finished), the countdown braking the car off the line, and loops drawn face-down so the car drove through them.\",\n    \"Three of them were game-breaking: no run could be driven, every run began with a respawn, and loops could not be driven at all.\",\n    \"The most helpful test was a bot run of every road that counts respawns, because it exposed the three critical bugs at once.\",\n    \"The least helpful test was the page's no-error check: it passed while the game was broken, and a silent canvas stub hid the look until screenshots were taken.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"The pen for code-drawn parts, the fixed camera, and the engine's menus, pause and settings were the best parts of the engine.\",\n    \"Stuck on the 3D track and vehicle: they don't drive a loop, and the boot runs asynchronously, so tests must await game.booted.\",\n    \"The road mesh and colliders, the car model, the bot, the run rules and every mode are my own; the engine supplied only the world, camera, menus and boot.\",\n    \"The hardest part was the 3D side's size and the headless canvas, which needed a stub before the world would build under Node.\",\n    \"Changed in the engine: E1 pen frame (any orientation), E2 camera up vector, E4 analog triggers, E5 PlayStation glyphs by default, E6 exported toon bands, each for a reason in the plan.\",\n    \"I would add one call that builds a racing road with a loop, or a documented road-mesh helper, since that is what this game needed most.\"\n  ],\n  \"promptFeedback\": [\n    \"The plan's detail on the car model, the controls and the validated physics appendix was the most useful part of the prompt.\",\n    \"The plan is sized for a far bigger build than one session; the title rule, where TASK.md wins, was clear.\",\n    \"The hardest thing was scope: the loop and the editor alone are each bigger than what this session could finish.\",\n    \"I would add a smaller first milestone and a note on what to cut first when time runs short.\"\n  ],\n  \"aiHub\": {\n    \"name\": \"CRACKMANIA\",\n    \"tagline\": \"Crack the clock.\",\n    \"description\": \"A desert time-attack racer: short roads of bends, hills and kicker jumps, with medals, ghosts, a survival gauntlet and hot-seat cups.\",\n    \"type\": \"Game\",\n    \"genre\": \"Racing\",\n    \"source\": \"TrackMania (2003)\",\n    \"series\": \"TrackMania\",\n    \"players\": \"1–4\",\n    \"controls\": \"R2/W gas, L2/S brake, left stick or arrows steer, Circle/Enter respawn, Triangle/R restart\",\n    \"tags\": [\"3d\", \"arcade\", \"vehicles\", \"retro\", \"low-poly\"]\n  }\n}\nEOF\nnode -e \"const j=JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8')); const need=['date','source','plan','genre','perspective','tech','artDirection','animation','audio','online','testing','research','environment','model','usage']; const miss=need.filter(k=>!j.sourceInformation[k]); console.log('parses; missing source fields:', miss.length ? miss : 'none', '| feedback counts', j.testingFeedback.length, j.engineFeedback.length, j.promptFeedback.length, '| aiHub tags', j.aiHub.tags.length)\" && cd Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050317 && timeout 900 node tools/test.mjs 2>&1 | grep -v deprecated | tail -4","description":"Write exit-interview.json, verify it parses, and run the tests"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":884,"cache_read_input_tokens":375990,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":884},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff784da1-c76f-414c-93e3-0cac44d8d956","uuid":"1323e7d8-e60e-4707-9916-c13c4d621703","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:26:36.733Z","request_id":"req_011CghtJfXQupxz6oF697WJC","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_016CdeyqL1hX1BBmMeVV827E":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050317__x1f94fb/work && cat > exit-interview.json <<'EOF'\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 05:03:17\",\