{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghtKxTRfpjm4j177Viv7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PTLR5jDwxoJ6ss28Btmpdz","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-haiku-5-5-medium.build__20261104-050317__x1f94fb/work/Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050317 && cat > engine/CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (base: my-3d2dge v0.85.2, commit 4390a98)\n\n| # | File | Change | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| E1 | my-3d2dge-3d.js, `Pen` | `frame(x, y, z, f, r, u, k)`: sets the pen's frame from forward, right and up vectors | draw the car in any orientation with no Euler singularity |\n| E2 | my-3d2dge-3d.js, `Camera3D.place()` | a fixed pose may carry `up` (engine axes); `roll` is skipped when `up` is given | a chase camera that keeps its up vector |\n| E4 | my-3d2dge.js, `Input` | `padValues` kept each step; `analog(action)` returns 0..1 (triggers) | analog R2 throttle and L2 brake |\n| E5 | my-3d2dge.js, `Input` and settings | PlayStation symbols by default; the Button symbols setting offers PlayStation and Xbox | the brief's glyph rule |\n| E6 | my-3d2dge-3d.js, statics | `World3D.TOON_BANDS` exported | game materials match the pen's parts |\n\nNot changed: the 2D and 3D engines' tracks and vehicles (they cannot drive a loop; the game has its own road mesh and car model).\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write the engine change log"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1612,"cache_read_input_tokens":379358,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1612},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff784da1-c76f-414c-93e3-