{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghtLRwu3JHpYUHG4ehhE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The goal is not met. I built a playable slice of CRACKMANIA, but TASK.md asks for a feature-complete demo, and large parts are missing.\n\n**What's delivered** (in the work folder)\n- `Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050317.html`: a single 4.5 MB file. It boots from `file://` with no page or console errors.\n- `exit-interview.json`: parses, and every field is filled.\n- The dev folder `Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-haiku-5-5-medium-20261104-050317/` holds the source, the build script, the test command (`node tools/test.mjs`), and `engine/CHANGES.md`.\n\n**Working**\n- Race on five desert roads: checkpoints in order, respawn to the last gate, restart, and a 3-2-1-GO countdown.\n- Medals (Author time from the bot's clean run), coppers, and a garage with six paints.\n- Ghost of your best run, with a split delta, and a replay from the results screen.\n- Survival: a five-road gauntlet against three rival bots.\n- Hot seat: two to four players on a three-road cup.\n- Title with a demo backdrop, and attract mode after 10 seconds idle. Any input exits.\n- Dev Mode from the pause menu: live sliders, bot-drive toggle, and reset to defaults.\n- Settings offer PlayStation or Xbox symbols, with PlayStation as the default.\n- A touch-only device sees \"Controller or keyboard required\".\n- About pages carry the source information and feedback.\n\n**Missing or not built**\n- Online (AI Hub ghost mode), split screen, and the track editor (Build).\n- Puzzle mode, and a replay list (replays are only reachable from the results screen).\n- Two more environments (only the Dustbowl exists), and 5 roads of the 15 planned.\n- Loops. My attempts drove through the road or left the car stuck on it, so I removed them from the track language.\n- Car engine sound and Animalese voices; music and effects are the engine's presets.\n- Story beats and tips (only a few Coco lines appear on the results screen).\n- Mouse control of the sliders (keyboard and pad only).\n- The sand reads as dark brown; the cause isn't confirmed.\n\n**Decisions I made**\n- Title is CRACKMANIA, as STAGE.md and the plan specify.\n- Medal times are computed at boot from the bot's run, not a baked file.\n- Attract mode is the bot driving, with no cheats.\n- The track is my own road mesh and car model, because the engine's track and vehicle can't drive a loop.\n\n**Verification:** 19 checks pass. The bot finishes all five roads with zero respawns. Scene flow works from title through results and retry. The engine changes E1, E2, E4, E5 and E6 are applied.\n\n**Next steps:** the remaining work is large. The most valuable next pieces are AI Hub online, the editor (which also unlocks puzzles), and the two other environments. Tell me whether to continue with those, or to stop here.\n\n---\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-04 05:03:17\n- Source: TrackMania 2003 (Nadeo)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: arcade time-attack racing; third-person chase camera, with an orbiting camera on the title and attract screens\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 2D engine and 3D engine v0.85.2; three.js r182; Rapier 0.19.3; esbuild 0.25.12; playwright-core 1.63.0 for checks\n- Art Direction: the engine's toon 3D style with ink outlines and pixel-art UI, all drawn by code\n- Animation: code-driven car, gate and camera motion; no rig animation\n- Audio: engine songs and effects, synthesised in code; no voices\n- Online: none\n- Testing: headless Node suites run by one command, plus Playwright boot and screenshot checks of the built file\n- Research: none\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about eight real bugs. Three were critical: the steering sign (no bot finished), the countdown braking the car off the line, and loops drawn face-down so the car drove through them.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** the same three. Together they meant no run could be driven, every run began with a respawn, and loops could not be driven at all.\n- **Most helpful test:** a bot run of every road that counts respawns. It exposed the three critical bugs at once.\n- **Least helpful test:** the page's no-error check. It passed while the game was broken, and a silent canvas stub hid the look until screenshots were taken.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the pen for code-drawn parts, the fixed camera, and the engine's menus, pause and settings.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** the 3D track and vehicle don't drive a loop, and boot runs asynchronously, so tests must await `game.booted`.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the road mesh and colliders, the car model, the bot, the run rules, and every mode.\n- **Hardest part:** the 3D side's size, and the headless canvas, which needed a stub before the world would build under Node.\n- **Engine changes:** E1 pen frame, E2 camera up vector, E4 analog triggers, E5 PlayStation glyphs by default, E6 exported toon bands. Each is logged in `engine/CHANGES.md`.\n- **One change I'd make:** one call that builds a racing road with a loop, or a documented road-mesh helper.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan's detail on the car model, the controls, and the validated physics appendix.\n- **Confusing:** the plan is sized for a far bigger build than one session. The title rule, where TASK.md wins, was clear.\n- **Hardest:** scope. The loop and the editor alone are each bigger than this session could finish.\n- **Would change:** a smaller first milestone, and a note on what to cut first when time runs short."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1538,"cache_read_input_tokens":380970,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1538},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff784da1-c76f-414c-93e3-0cac44d8d956","uuid":"85d4c68e-f2b3-44ae-95af-4e8c635fa5a4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:26:58.915Z","request_id":"req_011CghtLRaKrtGyAmnhkAVMb"}
