{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CghtpRk2CYxjYAT8vbg4u","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I kept building against TASK.md. Every TASK.md item now has a working version, but the plan's larger scope is still unbuilt, so the goal's \"feature-complete, no stubs\" bar is only partly met. The stop-hook condition is still not satisfied.\n\n**Added this round**\n- **AI Hub multiplayer (ghost mode, protocol v1):** all copies race the same road, chosen from the hub's seed. Each copy sends its car's pose and progress and reports its time once. Other players appear as ghost cars. A fake-hub test covers this path.\n- **Fifteen roads in three environments:** Dustbowl, Hedgerow, and Frostpeak, each with its own world, sky, and ground. The bot finishes all fifteen with zero respawns.\n- **Track editor (Build):** a piece palette, undo, test drive, and three save slots.\n- **Puzzles:** three puzzles with a piece budget and a distance goal. Each has a known solution that the test drives.\n- **Survival and hot seat:** the five-road gauntlet against three rival bots, and the hot-seat cup, both from the earlier round.\n- **Sound and voice:** a car engine tone driven by speed and throttle, and syllable babble for Coco. A first-run Coco intro plays on the title.\n- **Dev Mode:** sliders can be set by mouse click on their bars, and the touch-only path turns touch buttons off.\n\n**Verification:** `node tools/test.mjs` runs 23 checks, all passing. The built single file loads from `file://` with no errors. The About text and `exit-interview.json` are updated to match.\n\n**Still not built**\n- **Loops:** the TrackMania loop is not in the game. My attempts drove through the road or left the car stuck, so I dropped them. This is in the plan, not in TASK.md.\n- **Split screen:** plan item, not in TASK.md.\n- **Replay library:** replays are reachable only from the results screen.\n- **Story beats:** only the intro and the results lines exist.\n- **Per-environment cars and handling:** the same car runs in all three environments.\n- **Screenshots of the editor:** my navigation for that check missed, so I checked the editor through tests, not a picture.\n\nWant me to continue with loops and split screen, or stop here? Loops are the hardest part, so I'd need a decision on whether to keep trying them.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-04 05:03:17\n- Source: TrackMania 2003 (Nadeo)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: racing (arcade time attack) with track-building puzzles; third-person chase camera, with an orbiting camera on the title, attract, and editor screens\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 2D engine and 3D engine v0.85.2; three.js r182; Rapier 0.19.3; esbuild 0.25.12; playwright-core 1.63.0 for checks; AI Hub client session.js\n- Art Direction: the engine's toon 3D style with ink outlines and pixel-art UI, all drawn by code\n- Animation: code-driven car, gate, and camera motion; no rig animation\n- Audio: engine songs and effects; car engine tone and babble voices synthesised in code\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode (client 1.4.0)\n- Testing: 23 headless checks behind one command; Playwright boot and screenshot checks of the built file\n- Research: none\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about eight real bugs; three were critical. The steering sign (no bot finished), the countdown braking the car off the line, and loops drawn face-down so the car drove through them.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** those same three. No run could be driven, every run began with a respawn, and loops could not be driven at all.\n- **Most helpful test:** the bot finishing every road and counting respawns. It exposed the three critical bugs at once.\n- **Least helpful test:** the page's no-error check. It passed while the game was broken, and a silent canvas stub hid the look until screenshots were taken.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the pen for code-drawn parts, the fixed camera, and the engine's menus, pause, and settings.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** the engine's track and vehicle don't drive a loop, and boot is asynchronous, so tests must await `game.booted`.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** the road mesh and colliders, the car model, the bot, the run rules, and every mode.\n- **Hardest part:** the 3D side's size, and the headless canvas, which needed a stub before the world would build under Node.\n- **Engine changes:** E1 pen frame, E2 camera up vector, E4 analog triggers, E5 PlayStation glyphs by default, E6 exported toon bands. Logged in `engine/CHANGES.md`.\n- **One change I'd make:** one call that builds a racing road with a loop, or a documented road-mesh helper.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan's detail on the car model, the controls, and the validated physics appendix.\n- **Confusing:** the plan is sized for a much bigger build than one session. The title rule, where TASK.md wins, was clear.\n- **Hardest:** scope. The loop and the editor alone are each bigger than this session could finish.\n- **Would change:** a smaller first milestone, and a note on what to cut first when time runs short."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":828,"cache_read_input_tokens":454307,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":828},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff784da1-c76f-414c-93e3-0cac44d8d956","uuid":"6711ca2e-29fb-40ae-9ae1-b562efc24155","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:33:17.462Z","request_id":"req_011CghtpRPCMf84tVf54t1xV"}
