{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghu1JGNfs3Tr4xEMx2Pn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundled single-file build is in place and the scripted playthrough passes, but I can't honestly say every item is complete. The last loops attempt failed, and a few TASK.md areas are thin.\n\n**Done in this round**\n- **Per-environment handling:** Hedgerow has less grip, and Frostpeak has much less grip, less road hold, and softer steering. The same car runs everywhere, with these multipliers.\n- **Replay library:** a Replays menu on the title screen lists every road, and watches your best ghost on any road you've finished.\n- **Story beats:** Coco's first-finish talk and the Ghost Guild introduction before survival. Each plays once per profile.\n- **Scripted playthrough:** one test drives all 15 roads with the bot, then a replay, a puzzle solve, the five-road gauntlet, and a two-player hot-seat cup. It also checks for engine errors.\n\n**Verification:** 24 headless checks pass with `node tools/test.mjs`. The rebuilt single file loads from `file://` with zero errors.\n\n**What is still missing, honestly**\n- **Loops:** the TrackMania loop is not in the game. I tried twice, and the road model can't handle a loop cleanly. This is a PLAN.md item, not TASK.md.\n- **Split screen:** a PLAN.md item, not TASK.md. The hot seat is the local multiplayer I built.\n- **Story and animation depth:** story is a few dialog beats. Animation is code-driven car, gate, and camera motion, with no rig animation. Both are thin.\n- **Audio:** the engine tone and babble are basic. Music and effects are the engine's presets.\n- **Polish:** this is a vertical slice. Not every screen has been looked at in a browser.\n\nIf the stop hook needs every PLAN.md item, loops and split screen are the two that remain. I can keep working on them, but loops are the risky one.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-04 05:03:17\n- Source: TrackMania 2003 (Nadeo)\n- Plan: PLAN.md\n- Genre and Perspective: racing (arcade time attack) with track-building puzzles; third-person chase camera, with an orbiting camera on the title, attract, and editor screens\n- Tech: my-3D2dge 2D engine and 3D engine v0.85.2; three.js r182; Rapier 0.19.3; esbuild 0.25.12; playwright-core 1.63.0 for checks; AI Hub client session.js\n- Art Direction: the engine's toon 3D style with ink outlines and pixel-art UI, all drawn by code\n- Animation: code-driven car, gate, and camera motion; no rig animation\n- Audio: engine songs and effects; car engine tone and babble voices synthesised in code\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode (client 1.4.0)\n- Testing: 24 headless checks behind one command, including a scripted whole-game playthrough; Playwright boot and screenshot checks of the built file\n- Research: none\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-haiku-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **Issues caught:** about eight real bugs; three were critical. The steering sign (no bot finished), the countdown braking the car off the line, and loops drawn face-down so the car drove through them. Later, the first-finish dialog and the bot toggle reset broke two tests.\n- **Critical / game-breaking:** the three above. No run could be driven, every run began with a respawn, and loops could not be driven at all.\n- **Most helpful test:** the bot finishing every road and counting respawns. It exposed the critical bugs at once.\n- **Least helpful test:** the page's no-error check. It passed while the game was broken, and a silent canvas stub hid the look until screenshots were taken.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the pen for code-drawn parts, the fixed camera, and the engine's menus, pause, and settings.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** the engine's track and vehicle don't drive a loop, and boot is asynchronous, so tests must await `game.booted`.\n- **Most important thing I built myself:** the road mesh and colliders, the car model, the bot, the run rules, and every mode.\n- **Hardest part:** the 3D side's size, and the headless canvas, which needed a stub before the world would build under Node.\n- **Engine changes:** E1 pen frame, E2 camera up vector, E4 analog triggers, E5 PlayStation glyphs by default, E6 exported toon bands. Logged in `engine/CHANGES.md`.\n- **One change I'd make:** one call that builds a racing road with a loop, or a documented road-mesh helper.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan's detail on the car model, the controls, and the validated physics appendix.\n- **Confusing:** the plan is sized for a much bigger build than one session. The title rule, where TASK.md wins, was clear.\n- **Hardest:** scope. A loop road and a split screen are each still bigger than this session could finish.\n- **Would change:** a smaller first milestone, and a note on what to cut first when time runs short."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1191,"cache_read_input_tokens":471894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1191},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff784da1-c76f-414c-93e3-0cac44d8d956","uuid":"7c31a2fd-767a-451e-99a8-b310f3a3d011","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:35:45.853Z","request_id":"req_011Cghu1Hw3CSKB9nJSziPH4"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The condition requires every feature in TASK.md to be implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. The last assistant message explicitly states 'I can't honestly say every item is complete' and lists unbuilt items: loops ('the TrackMania loop is not in the game'), split screen, thin story and animation ('Both are thin'), basic audio, and unreviewed polish ('Not every screen has been looked at in a browser'). The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json exist and the four feedback sections are present, but feature completeness is not met."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff784da1-c76f-414c-93e3-0cac44d8d956","uuid":"146b2146-4d7f-4b6a-9c7b-52472295d933","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:35:47.894Z","isSynthetic":true}
